[agent] **What I did:**
[agent] 1. **Identified the right interface** — `hops agent` deploys a local `.py` script as a server-only (model-less) real-time deployment served over the platform's inference path.
[agent] 2. **Discovered the contract from the SDK source** — agent scripts are *run directly* (not imported as a `Predict` class), so the script must start its own HTTP server on port `8080` and speak the KServe v1 protocol (`POST /v1/models/<name>:predict`). My first attempt used the `Predict`-class contract; the pod came up but never bound 8080 (`aggressive probe error … connection refused`), which confirmed the run-directly model.
